<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Each curve below has a stationary point at <m>x = 0</m>. Choose the nature of that stationary point.</p><div><m>y = {x^4}</m>: [ maximum point | minimum point | point of inflection ]  </div><div><m>y = {x^3}</m>: [ maximum point | minimum point | point of inflection ]  </div><div><m>y = {-3 x^2}</m>: [ maximum point | minimum point | point of inflection ]  </div><div><m>y = {x^3+2 x^2}</m>: [ maximum point | minimum point | point of inflection ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>If <m>\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} \gt 0</m> at a stationary point it is a minimum point; if <m>\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} \lt 0</m> it is a maximum point. If <m>\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 0</m> the test is silent, not a verdict: test the sign of <m>\dfrac{dy}{dx}</m> either side instead.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Curve</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>\dfrac{dy}{dx}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}</m> at <m>x = 0</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Signs of <m>\dfrac{dy}{dx}</m> at <m>x = -0.1</m> and <m>x = 0.1</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Nature</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y = {x^4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4 x^3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>-</m>, <m>+</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">minimum point</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y = {x^3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3 x^2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>+</m>, <m>+</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">point of inflection</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y = {-3 x^2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-6 x}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">not needed</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">maximum point</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y = {x^3+2 x^2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3 x^2+4 x}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">not needed</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">minimum point</cell></row></tabular><p>A sign pattern <m>-, +</m> means a minimum point, <m>+, -</m> a maximum point, and the same sign on both sides a point of inflection.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>minimum point</p></answer>
    <answer><p>point of inflection</p></answer>
    <answer><p>maximum point</p></answer>
    <answer><p>minimum point</p></answer>
</stack-static>